---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import { site, contact } from '../../data/site';
---
<Base
  title="About | Joshua Abrogena"
  description="Who I am, what I have built and when, how I work, and what this portfolio does not claim."
>
  <div class="container wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>{site.name}</h1>
    <p class="lede">Backend systems and AWS infrastructure.</p>

    <Section id="who" title="Who I am">
      <p>My work focuses on the parts of a system where things go wrong: a payment that arrives twice, a worker killed halfway through a job, two buyers reaching for the last pair. I build backends in Java and Go, deploy them to AWS with Terraform, and write down what I tested and what I did not.</p>
      <p>The work on this site is two projects: a payments and inventory store, and a crash-safe video platform. Neither has users or clients. They are how I show what I can do, so each one states its status and its limits.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="work" title="What I have built, and when">
      <ul class="timeline">
        <li><strong>RyuZCloud</strong>, a video platform. Crash-recovery tests on 2026-11-10, a first AWS session on 2026-11-14, a seeded library and frontend measurements from 2026-11-24 to 2026-11-26. Live at ryuzcloud.com. <a href="/projects/ryuzcloud/">Case study</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>RyuStoreFront</strong>, a payments and inventory store. Concurrency and webhook tests from 2026-11-14, AWS sessions on 2026-11-15 and 2026-11-23. Live at ryustorefront.com. Still in development. <a href="/projects/ryustorefront/">Case study</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These dates come from each project's own metrics ledger. They show when the work was recorded, not how many hours it took.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section id="how-i-work" title="How I work">
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Decide scope and tradeoffs.</strong> Each project keeps a decision log that records what was chosen and what it cost.</li>
        <li><strong>Run the consequential commands myself.</strong> I run the Git, AWS and Terraform commands, and every apply runs from a saved plan that I read first.</li>
        <li><strong>Treat code as unverified until it is tested.</strong> Results are labelled by how they were obtained: run, user-reported or not run.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep a ledger of numbers.</strong> Every number on this site comes from a row in the project's own metrics file, with its setup, date and status, and says whether it was measured locally or on AWS. Estimates are left out.</li>
        <li><strong>Record what did not work.</strong> A change that made things worse is written down and reverted, not hidden.</li>
      </ul>
    </Section>

    <Section id="experience" title="Education and resume">
      <h3>Education</h3>
      <p>Computer Engineering at the University of Hawaiʻi at Mānoa, expected Fall 2026.</p>
      <h3>Resume</h3>
      {contact.resumeUrl
        ? <p><a href={contact.resumeUrl}>Resume (PDF)</a></p>
        : <p class="placeholder">Resume: to be added.</p>}
    </Section>

    <Section id="not" title="What this portfolio does not claim">
      <ul>
        <li>No clients, revenue, users or paid work.</li>
        <li>No scale, load or uptime figures. Both projects are live, but no number on this site was measured on the current deployments.</li>
        <li>No real payments: RyuStoreFront runs Stripe in test mode only.</li>
        <li>No results beyond what each project's own records show. Where I could not re-check a result I say so.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a href="/projects/">See the projects</a> &middot; <a href="/contact/">Contact</a></p>
    </Section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap { padding-block: var(--space-8) 0; }
  h1 { font-size: var(--step-5); margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .lede { color: var(--color-text-muted); font-size: var(--step-1); margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-7); }
  .timeline { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); }
  .placeholder { color: var(--color-text-muted); }
</style>
